{"question_id": "505af2f5", "hypothesis": "Step 1 \u2014 Extract relevant information from the history\n- You already make a flavored creamer with unsweetened almond milk, vanilla extract, and honey.\n- You wanted tips earlier on making it healthier (less sugar, alternate sweeteners, spices, different milks, add-ins like protein/MCT/collagen).\n- You\u2019ve shown interest in seasonal/bright flavors (e.g., Lemon Ginger from earlier coffee-flavor chat) and in lowering sugar/calories.\n\nStep 2 \u2014 Reasoning\n- Goal: give new creamer ideas that (a) build on your almond-milk base, (b) offer healthier or more interesting flavor/texture options, and (c) remain simple to make and store.\n- Approaches: 1) swap/limit sweetener (monk fruit/stevia/yacon or less honey); 2) boost creaminess with cashew/coconut/soaked-nut creams rather than more sugar; 3) add flavor via spices, zest, extracts, or infused syrups; 4) add functional add-ins (collagen, MCT, protein) if desired.\n- Practical constraints: small batches first, refrigerate, shake before use, label and date.\n\nStep 3 \u2014 Recommendations (recipes and quick tips)\nMake each recipe in a jar, shake/blend until smooth. All recipes yield ~1 cup.\n\n1) Simple Low-Sugar Vanilla-Almond (everyday)\n- 1 cup unsweetened almond milk\n- 1 tsp pure vanilla extract\n- 1\u20132 tsp monk-fruit or 1/2\u20131 tsp liquid stevia (or 1 tsp honey if you prefer)\n- Pinch of salt\nMethod: Whisk or shake. Use for regular coffee. Store refrigerated 5\u20137 days.\n\n2) Creamy Cashew-Almond (richer, still vegan)\n- 1/2 cup unsweetened almond milk + 1/2 cup cashew cream (blend 1/3 cup soaked cashews + 1/2 cup water until silky)\n- 1 tsp maple syrup (or 1 tsp yacon syrup)\n- 1 tsp vanilla extract\nMethod: Blend until smooth. Thicker, very creamy. Refrigerate 5\u20137 days.\n\n3) Coconut Mocha (indulgent, dairy-free)\n- 3/4 cup light coconut milk (canned, shaken) + 1/4 cup almond milk\n- 1 tsp cocoa powder (dissolve in a bit of hot water first)\n- 1 tsp maple syrup or 1/2 tsp honey\n- 1/2 tsp vanilla\nMethod: Whisk or blend. Great in iced coffee. Store refrigerated 4\u20136 days.\n\n4) Lemon-Ginger Spring Cremer (bright \u2014 good with cold brew)\n- 1 cup almond milk\n- 1 tsp lemon zest (or 1 tbsp mild lemon syrup)\n- 1/4\u20131/2 tsp freshly grated ginger (or 1/2 tsp ginger syrup)\n- 1 tsp honey or 1/2 tsp monk fruit\n- Pinch salt\nMethod: Warm gently to infuse 5\u201310 min, strain out solids, cool. (Citrus can sometimes curdle in very hot coffee; best with cold brew or add to cup after diluting coffee slightly.) Refrigerate 3\u20135 days.\n\n5) Spiced Cardamom-Cinnamon (cozy)\n- 1 cup almond or oat milk\n- 1/2 tsp ground cinnamon + 1/8 tsp ground cardamom (or 2 crushed green cardamom pods steeped)\n- 1 tsp vanilla\n- 1 tsp maple syrup or honey (optional)\nMethod: Warm lightly to bloom spices, strain if using whole pods. Refrigerate 5\u20137 days.\n\n6) Functional Boost (MCT / Collagen)\n- 1 cup almond milk\n- 1 tbsp MCT oil (or coconut oil)\n- 1 scoop collagen peptides (if non-vegan) or a plant protein powder\n- 1 tsp vanilla and sweetener to taste\nMethod: Blend well (oil emulsifies better with a blender). Use in coffee that you stir/blend. Store refrigerated 3\u20135 days. Shake/blend before each use.\n\nExtra tips\n- Start with small batches (1 cup) to test flavors.\n- Use full-fat coconut milk or cashew cream for the creamiest mouthfeel without added sugar.\n- If you want a stable texture in hot coffee, blend (immersion blender) to emulsify, or add a small pinch of sunflower lecithin (optional).\n- Freeze extra creamer in ice-cube trays for single-serve portions (good for 1 month).\n- Label with date and ingredients; discard if smell/taste changes.\n\nIf you tell me which direction you prefer (low-sugar, ultra-creamy, seasonal, or functional), I can give a single optimized recipe and exact step-by-step instructions.", "autoeval_label": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "label": true}}
