inimize cleanup.\n\nWeekly & monthly deep-clean tasks\n- Weekly: fridge quick clean (toss expired items), microwave wipe, sweep & mop floors, wipe cabinet fronts.  \n- Monthly: clean oven, degrease range hood filter, descale kettle/coffee maker, deep clean disposal.  \n- Every few months: declutter pantry, check seals on containers, re-seal granite if recommended.\n\nKeep cleaning simple with the right supplies\n- Microfiber cloths, a spray bottle of warm water + dish soap, a granite-safe cleaner, baking soda, white vinegar (for general cleaning/odors), soft scrub pads, and garbage/compost liners.  \n- Keep a small stash of essential supplies under the sink or in a caddy so cleaning is always convenient.\n\nMotivation & routine\n- Set a recurring 10\u201315 minute reminder each evening for the kitchen reset.  \n- Pair reset time with something pleasant (music or a podcast) so it becomes a habit.  \n- Celebrate small wins \u2014 a clean counter and empty sink makes the whole kitchen feel better.\n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Create a 7\u2011day quick-clean checklist you can print or add to your phone, or  \n- Suggest an optimized layout for your utensil holder and counter to minimize clutter.\n\nWhich would you prefer?", "autoeval_label": {"model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "label": true}}
